## Invariants

Numbered, falsifiable; Technical Architecture I-nn cited where one exists. No runtime code exists in this checkout, so none of these holds today and none is covered by a test.

1. Resolving an external key that already exists in the same `(connectorNamespace, scopeKey, keyKind)` returns the existing `OriginRecord` and creates no second record. *[Blueprint §28; no I-nn]*
2. An `origin_revision` row cannot be modified after insert: an `UPDATE` through the runtime or through test SQL is refused. *[I-06]*
3. No runtime query or stored column treats `external_version_key` as ordered; given two version keys with no connector precedence instruction, neither is "newer". *[Blueprint §30, §63; no I-nn]*
4. Given the same version key with a divergent payload digest, the stored revision is preserved bit-for-bit and an `identity_conflict` row exists afterwards. *[Blueprint §44; no I-nn]*
5. An ambiguous alias never removes an `origin_record`, never rewrites an `external_identity` row that already pointed at another record, and always leaves an `ambiguous_alias` conflict behind. *[Blueprint §27]*
6. No `source_membership` row exists without an explicit membership claim, and inserting a `target_observation` never inserts a membership. *[Blueprint §36, §37]*
7. No `source` row has `id = 0`, and every table holding a local identity refuses `0` (D3). *[Technical Architecture §8]*
8. Every value crossing from catalog/legacy into a runtime ID passes the checked conversion; no `UInt32(...)`/`UInt64(...)` narrowing appears in `FeedDomain`, `FeedStorage` or `feedmine/RuntimeV2`. *[Technical Architecture §8]*
9. External identity equality is decided by comparing the full key bytes; a digest equality without full-key equality never joins two records, and the digest is never the only stored key. *[Technical Architecture §9]*
10. Deleting connector evidence cannot change identity resolution: the resolution inputs are rows in `external_identity`, not evidence payloads. *[I-16]*
11. After a catalog rebuild, every previously mapped `legacy_source_map` row still resolves to the same `runtime_source_id`, and no runtime source is created, deleted or renumbered by row order. *[plan §5.1]*
12. No row has `authored_at` derived from `observed_at` or from the current clock; a revision admitted without an authored timestamp keeps `authored_at IS NULL`. *[Blueprint §35]*
13. A revision with `headline IS NULL` or `primary_link IS NULL` can be admitted, selected and published; no synthetic HTTP URL is ever written into `primary_link`. *[Blueprint §33, §34]*
14. Two admissions with distinct fallback keys produce two `origin_record` rows even when title and authored date are identical; neither payload replaces the other. *[plan §5.1, Blueprint §44]*
15. Removing `content_entity_member`/`content_cluster_member` rows leaves every original `origin_record` and revision intact and individually selectable. *[Blueprint §39, §40]*
16. A `content_relation` row only ever carries one of the four promoted relations; any other external relation appears in no canonical table. *[Blueprint §41, §42]*
17. A `provider_attribution` row never changes `source_membership` and never changes a `SourceID`; provider identity is never substituted for source identity in any keyed lookup. *[Blueprint §21, §38]*
18. While the ADR-004 compatibility window is open, no bookmark, collection or history row is keyed by a runtime integer ID; each carries the legacy durable key or a snapshot. *[I-16, plan §5.2]*
19. An external key spelled like a URL is stored byte-identical to what the connector supplied: no scheme rewrite, no parameter removal, no host normalization, no relative resolution. *[Blueprint §27; D10]*
20. A revoked/disabled binding or source keeps its `source` and `external_identity` rows; disablement changes eligibility, never identity. *[I-12 for the admission half; ADR-006, ADR-005]*

## Edge cases

- Catalog rebuild where a source disappeared, was renamed, or merged: mappings are re-applied by key; unmatched runtime sources are retained (identity is never deleted by a rebuild), and ambiguous catalog claims become `legacy_map_conflict` rows instead of a silent re-point.
- Canonicalization version bump: the same URL can yield a different `editorial_key` under a new version. Continuity must be declared in `legacy_source_map`; without a declaration, a new `source` row is created and the divergence is recorded, never merged by URL similarity.
- Signed/expiring feed URLs: identity stripping is legitimate for the *source/fetch* URL (`CatalogIdentityContractTests.swift:42-47`) and forbidden for external object keys (D10), including equivalent `X-Amz-*`/`temp_url_sig` forms.
- The same GUID appearing under two accounts, two feeds, or two connector namespaces: two `origin_record` rows, because scope is part of the key space.
- GUID that is a valid URL on a host also used by another source: no host merging; the byte string is the key.
- 128-bit digest collision: detection triggers a full-key comparison and writes `digest_collision`; the colliding keys remain distinct.
- Versionless observations (`external_version_key IS NULL`) of the same record: deduplicate by payload digest; a changed payload admits a new revision and never rewrites the previous one.
- Same version key, divergent payload (D11): existing revision untouched, conflict recorded, incoming revision admitted under a new key or rejected with a typed refusal (ADR-006) — the choice must be one of the two, never a silent overwrite.
- Alias arriving after the record is established, alias already owned by another record, and two records claiming the same alias: all three are `ambiguous_alias` and leave both records intact.
- Item with no GUID and no link, title present: low-confidence fallback key (D16). Two items sharing title/date: two records. Neither is dropped.
- Legacy path currently drops titleless items (`RSSFetcher.swift:967`) and linkless items (`:960`): Runtime V2 must admit both, and the mirrored shadow comparison must classify these as *legacy gap*, not as runtime divergence.
- Crash between revision insert and `current_revision_id` CAS: recovery re-runs admission; `current_revision_id` still points at the previous revision, and no duplicate revision appears (ADR-006 owns the CAS).
- Clock skew: `authored_at` in the future or far before `observed_at` is stored as declared and flagged in the observation; it is never clamped or replaced (D17).
- Legacy item row deleted by retention while its bookmark survives (`FeedStore.swift:7256-7261`): `legacy_item_map` may keep the mapping; hydration depends on the ADR-004 snapshot, not on `feed_item`.
- `user.sqlite` unavailable or migrating during a runtime write: mappings and conflicts persist in `runtime-v2.sqlite`; bridge operations stay additive and re-appliable (plan §5.2).
- Migration from a database created before this ADR: unmapped legacy ids resolve to `unresolved`, never to a guessed source; `legacy_item_map.confidence` records it.
- Revoked binding with an in-flight stream: identity rows stay, stale batches are refused at admission (I-12), and no membership is created retrospectively.

## Named acceptance tests

> **Where these live, checked 2026-09-18.** The names in this list are the plan §19 criteria; the *paths* were written before the tests landed, so a path is a plan until it resolves. One here is still a planned name: `feedmineTests/RuntimeV2LegacyMapperTests` exists as `feedmineTests/LegacyIdentityMapperTests.swift`. The rest resolve as written.

All of the following were written as **proposed** names and criteria from plan §19. **Checked 2026-09-18: they are proposals no longer.** The criteria are implemented and pinned by real tests — the mapping this list's paths need is in the note above, and the row-by-row binding is `contract-matrix.md`'s invariant table plus `baseline.md` §8.54.

- `sourceCanHaveMultipleBindings` — one Source row stays current while two bindings of different connector namespaces are admitted and enabled, and each binding carries its own generation — `FeedDomainTests` (D5, D6; plan row 1).
- `endpointChangePreservesSourceIdentity` — changing a binding's endpoint and config keeps `SourceID` and bumps only `binding.generation`, with no new `source` row — `FeedDomainTests`/`FeedStorageTests` (D6; row 2).
- `oneSourceContainsMultipleProviders` — several provider attributions across two revisions of one source coexist without collapsing provider identity into the Source — `FeedDomainTests` (D5; row 3).
- `bindingChangeInvalidatesOldGeneration` — a batch produced under the previous binding generation is refused at admission while the binding row remains usable at the new generation — `FeedStorageTests` (D6, cross-cited by ADR-006; row 4).
- `targetIsIndependentOfSourceIdentity` — sharing one target between two bindings of two Sources creates no shared or rewritten editorial identity — `FeedStorageTests` (D7, owned by ADR-005; row 5).
- `sameExternalKeyResolvesSameRecord` — admitting the same full key twice creates exactly one `origin_record` and no duplicate identity row (integrity check for the unique constraint) — `FeedStorageTests` (D8, row 7).
- `revisionPayloadCannotBeUpdated` — an attempted `UPDATE` of `origin_revision` fails through the runtime and through direct test SQL — `FeedStorageTests` (D11, I-06; row 8).
- `versionKeyIsNotAssumedGloballyOrdered` — two records with version keys in "decreasing" lexical/numeric order keep the connector's precedence instruction as the only ordering input; no query orders by version key — `FeedStorageTests` (D9; row 9).
- `ambiguousAliasDoesNotMergeOrigins` — a key claimed by two records produces an `ambiguous_alias` conflict, keeps both records, and rewrites neither identity row — `FeedStorageTests` (D12; row 10).
- `targetObservationDoesNotImplyMembership` — an observation through a shared target creates no `source_membership` row, and a membership created explicitly creates no observation — `FeedStorageTests` (D15; row 11).
- `clusterSplitPreservesOriginalRecords` — deleting cluster/entity membership rows leaves every original record and revision selectable with its provenance intact — `FeedStorageTests` (D13; row 12).
- `unknownExternalRelationStaysEvidence` — an external relation outside the four promoted verbs writes no `content_relation` row and remains available only as evidence — `FeedDomainTests` (D14; row 13).
- `missingAuthoredAtDoesNotBecomeClaimedPublicationDate` — a revision admitted without an authored timestamp keeps `authored_at IS NULL` and the fallback sort date is reported as a fallback, not as an authored date — `FeedDomainTests` (D17; row 14).
- `invalidBatchDoesNotMutateCanonicalState` — a batch with an invalid target stamp/revision payload leaves identity, membership, attribution, relation and checkpoint tables byte-identical — `FeedStorageTests` (D1, D11, D15; row 28, owned by ADR-005/006).
- `digestCollisionComparesFullExternalKey` — two keys sharing a digest are stored and resolved as different identities because full-key comparison decides — `FeedStorageTests` (D8, invariant 9).
- `opaqueGuidIsNotUrlNormalized` — a GUID that looks like a URL with signed query parameters is stored byte-identical, and two GUIDs differing only in parameters stay distinct — `FeedConnectorSyndicationTests` (D10, invariant 19).
- `catalogRebuildReappliesPersistedSourceMap` — rebuilding the catalog re-applies `legacy_source_map` and no runtime source id changes; a source present only in the old catalog is retained — `feedmineTests/RuntimeV2LegacyMapperTests` (D4, D18; invariant 11).
- `zeroSourceIDIsNotPersistable` — inserting id `0` into any identity table fails the CHECK, and the checked encoder refuses `0` and negatives — `FeedStorageTests` (D3; invariant 7).
- `versionlessObservationDoesNotDuplicateRevision` — two versionless observations with an identical payload digest produce one revision, and a changed payload produces a second immutable revision — `FeedStorageTests` (D9, D11; invariant 2).
- `identicalTitleAndDateFallbackKeepsBothRecords` — two linkless, GUID-less items with identical title and authored date produce two records with low-confidence fallback keys and no overwrite — `FeedStorageTests` (D16; invariant 14).
- `headlineAndLinkMayBeAbsent` — a revision with `headline IS NULL` and `primary_link IS NULL` is admitted, selected and published with no synthesized URL, where the legacy path dropped it (`RSSFetcher.swift:960,967`) — `FeedDomainTests` (D16, D18; Blueprint §33, §34).
- `providerAttributionNeverSubstitutesForSource` — a revision attributed to two providers leaves source membership and any source-keyed lookup unchanged — `FeedStorageTests` (D5; invariant 17).

